## solutions

#### depth first

```js
const hasPath = (graph, src, dst) => {
  if (src === dst) return true;

  for (let neighbor of graph[src]) {
    if (hasPath(graph, neighbor, dst) === true) {
      return true;
    }
  }

  return false;
};
```

- n = number of nodes
- e = number edges
- Time: O(e)
- Space: O(n)

#### breadth first

```js
const hasPath = (graph, src, dst) => {
  const queue = [src];

  while (queue.length) {
    const current = queue.shift();
    if (current === dst) return true;

    for (let neighbor of graph[current]) {
      queue.push(neighbor);
    }
  }

  return false;
};
```

- n = number of nodes
- e = number edges
- Time: O(e)
- Space: O(n)

Note: the JavaScript _shift()_ methods runs in linear time, so the complexity is really _O(e^2)_.

